slang: elaborate both instance bodies before comparing their parameters

A false "cyclic dependency found when determining value of 'W'" on legal
code: comparing a virtual interface type with a cached duplicate instance's
interface reads a derived parameter, whose lookup elaborates the body,
which resolves the port types, which need the same parameter.

Local issue SL-1 (patches/slang/README.md). Not reported upstream yet.
Present in v11.0 and v12.0. Applies to v11.0.

--- a/source/ast/symbols/InstanceSymbols.cpp
+++ b/source/ast/symbols/InstanceSymbols.cpp
@@ -1140,6 +1140,13 @@
     if (&definition != &other.definition)
         return false;
 
+    // Elaborate both bodies before reading their parameters. A parameter's
+    // initializer looks names up in its body, and the first lookup into an
+    // unelaborated body runs finishElaboration(), which resolves port types and
+    // so may need the very parameter being evaluated: a false cycle.
+    ensureElaborated();
+    other.ensureElaborated();
+
     auto getSym = std::views::transform([](auto& paramBase) { return &paramBase->symbol; });
     return ParameterSymbolBase::allMatching(parameters | getSym, other.parameters | getSym);
 }
